      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Idaho?",
      "a": "Idaho received $3.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 8,764 awards with an average award size of $379K. Obligations fell 15.5% year over year, and the fiscal-year series shows FY25 at $3.9B and FY26 at $3.3B to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Idaho?",
      "a": "The Department of Energy awards the most contracts in Idaho, obligating $2.5B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Agriculture follows with $429M and the Department of Defense follows with $172M. Other buying agencies in the top 10 include the Department of the Interior at $119M and the Department of Transportation at $26.3M."
